=== Notes added in GOLLUM (user/ricardo/nnlo_reweighting), not from the authors ===

Order of the scale variations (not given above; inferred from the LO totals, which factorise as
alpha_s^2(muR) * PDF(muF): var2 = var4 * var3 and var1 = var5 * var6 to 0.1%; to be confirmed with Rene):
  scale_var1 = (muR, muF) = (2, 2)
  scale_var2 = (0.5, 0.5)
  scale_var3 = (1, 0.5)
  scale_var4 = (0.5, 1)
  scale_var5 = (2, 1)
  scale_var6 = (1, 2)
The envelope of central + var1..var6 reproduces scale_up/scale_down of data-for-CMS-PAS-TOP-20-006-mt172.5 exactly.

Added PDF columns (NNLO files only), appended after mcerr_var6 by diagnostics/add_pdf_columns_to_stripper_variations.py:
  PDF_up PDF_down                         : absolute, copied from data-for-CMS-PAS-TOP-20-006-mt172.5 (pb/[X]...)
  PDF_up_normalized PDF_down_normalized   : copied from data-for-CMS-PAS-TOP-20-006-mt172.5-norm (1/[X]...)
The normalised PDF band cannot be rebuilt from the absolute up/down columns (the PDF members were normalised
individually), hence both are kept. The original columns are unchanged; the original files are in
/scratch/users/ricardo.barrue/stripper_variations_backup_20261127.tar.gz.

Normalisation: dividing every scale choice by its own total cross section, taken as the integral of the 1D pTttbar
distribution of the same scale choice (full phase space), reproduces the normalised files of
data-for-CMS-PAS-TOP-20-006-mt172.5-norm to 1e-4, also for the 2D and 3D distributions.
